<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthias von Jagow</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–1544</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthias von Jagow was the last Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, from 1526 to 1544. When Elector Joachim II introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in Brandenburg in 1539, the bishop accepted the change and took communion in both kinds. After his death the prince-bishopric was administered by Lutheran princes of the Hohenzollern house and finally absorbed into the electorate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matthias-von-jagow.jpg" alt="Matthias von Jagow" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo:gregor rom, sculpture: Harro Magnussen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%BCste_matthias_von_jagow.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
